# css-doctor project rules

Read `AGENTS.md` for the canonical guide and use the skills in
`.agents/skills/` for focused workflows.

- Monorepo: Rust core + NAPI binding + TS CLI/Vite/Next packages.
- Default file/folder naming is kebab-case. Exceptions: Rust module files
  (snake_case), Next route files, tool configs, generated files, and standard
  docs. React component filenames are kebab-case; identifiers stay PascalCase.
- Use Turborepo for workspace-wide tasks: `pnpm build`, `pnpm test`,
  `pnpm lint`, `pnpm check`, `pnpm format`, `pnpm test:cargo`.
- Graph: binding → CLI/Vite/Next → examples/vite-react-tailwind.
- Inspect order with `pnpm exec turbo build --dry-run`.
- For focused work: `pnpm --filter <pkg> typecheck|build|test`, but build the
  native binding before TypeScript integration tests.
- Never edit generated artifacts:
  - `packages/binding/index.js`, `index.d.ts`, `index.d.cts`, `*.node`
  - `packages/*/dist/**`, `.next/**`, `target/**`, coverage
- Do not add hand-written `.js`/`.cjs`/`.mjs` source. TypeScript and Rust only.
- Preserve error boundaries in Vite/Next; diagnostics must not crash builds.
- Page CSS chunks are emitted but not auto-linked into HTML/manifests yet.
- Before handoff run the relevant checks plus `git status`; no generated files.
